Rule 1 (Input dtype must be supported: bool, integer, float, or complex)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 0 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 5 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10
>>
Rule 2 (All dimension sizes are non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then true else ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 3 (Boolean tensors contain only 0/1 values)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 0 then min(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 1
>>
Rule 4 (Scalars and higher-dimensional tensors are allowed)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0
